ouse-that-rotates-320-degrees-using-two-washing-machine-motors-63-years-later-it-is-on-the-market-for-the-first-time/articleshow/133354983.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/in-1963-a-california-builder-made-a-house-that-rotates-320-degrees-using-two-washing-machine-motors-63-years-later-it-is-on-the-market-for-the-first-time/articleshow/133354983.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T00:43:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133358200,imgsize-1019892.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian caregiver fatally stabbed in Israel, elderly couple’s grandson indicted]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133354364.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/indian-caregiver-fatally-stabbed-in-israel-elderly-couples-grandson-indicted/articleshow/133354364.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/indian-caregiver-fatally-stabbed-in-israel-elderly-couples-grandson-indicted/articleshow/133354364.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T22:40:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133354686,imgsize-662735.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At least 100 killed after illegal gold mine collapses in Central African Republic]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133356183.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/at-least-100-killed-after-illegal-gold-mine-collapses-in-central-african-republic/articleshow/133356183.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/at-least-100-killed-after-illegal-gold-mine-collapses-in-central-african-republic/articleshow/133356183.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T23:23:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133356287,imgsize-347806.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Natalie Muro, 18-year-old Colorado student who used an invasive plant to fight algal blooms]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133353123.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable eighteen-year-old student has developed an ingenious device aimed at eradicating toxic algal blooms. Utilizing wind-driven waves and invasive plant species, this unique system demonstrated impressive results in field tests, removing nearly all cyanobacteria and trapping decayed cell matter. This groundbreaking solution offers a cost-effective way to restore and revitalize unhealthy freshwater ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-natalie-muro-the-18-year-old-colorado-student-who-used-wind-driven-waves-and-an-invasive-plant-to-fight-toxic-algal-blooms-in-a-real-reservoir/articleshow/133353123.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-natalie-muro-the-18-year-old-colorado-student-who-used-wind-driven-waves-and-an-invasive-plant-to-fight-toxic-algal-blooms-in-a-real-reservoir/articleshow/133353123.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T21:49:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133353529,imgsize-760522.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1958, the US secretly detonated 3 nuclear devices 100–500 km above the South Atlantic]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133352716.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a clandestine effort, Operation Argus conducted nuclear tests in the stratosphere over the South Atlantic Ocean. These detonations resulted in spectacular artificial auroras and fleeting radiation belts around our planet. The mission’s intent was to shield against Soviet missile threats and radar detection systems. Yet, the swift vanishing of these barriers caused significant communication disturbances, leading to the formulation of international accords banning nuclear experiments in space.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/1958-the-us-secretly-detonated-3-nuclear-devices-100500-km-above-the-south-atlantic-they-created-artificial-auroras-and-radiation-belts-that-lasted-weeks/articleshow/133352716.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/1958-the-us-secretly-detonated-3-nuclear-devices-100500-km-above-the-south-atlantic-they-created-artificial-auroras-and-radiation-belts-that-lasted-weeks/articleshow/133352716.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T21:24:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133352923,imgsize-970022.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 9-year-old girl in the Philippines raised money to help one of the world's rarest birds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133342965.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-9-year-old-girl-in-the-philippines-raised-money-to-help-one-of-the-worlds-rarest-birds-the-child-became-an-unlikely-conservation-campaigner/articlesh